    "slug": "what-is-included-in-social-media-management-dubai",
    "excerpt": "Social media management in Dubai should include strategy, content planning, creative production, publishing, community management, reporting and clear conversion paths.",
    "content": "<p><strong>Social media management in Dubai usually includes strategy, monthly content planning, creative direction, post and reel production, publishing, community management, reporting, and recommendations for paid promotion.</strong> Strong packages also connect social content to WhatsApp, booking, lead forms, landing pages and sales follow-up.</p><h2>What does a social media agency manage?</h2><p>A good agency manages the operating system behind social growth: audience research, content pillars, campaign calendar, captions, design, reels, photography, scheduling, comments, DMs, analytics and monthly optimisation. For brands in Dubai, the work often needs English and Arabic sensitivity, UAE cultural context, location signals, creator awareness and platform-specific execution.</p><p>Talk The Taste provides this through <a href=\"/social-media-marketing-dubai\">social media marketing in Dubai</a>.</p><h2>Core deliverables to expect</h2><ul><li>Brand, audience and competitor review.</li><li>Monthly content calendar with themes, formats and campaign dates.</li><li>Creative production for reels, carousels, stories and static posts.</li><li>Caption writing, hashtags, geotags and publishing.</li><li>Community management for comments, DMs and basic response flows.</li><li>Monthly reporting with content learnings and next actions.</li></ul><h2>Social media management vs social media marketing</h2><p>Management keeps the channels consistent and professional. Marketing goes further by connecting content to commercial outcomes: lead generation, offers, paid ads, influencer collaborations, landing pages, conversion tracking and customer retention. A brand that needs sales, bookings or enquiries should not buy posting alone.</p><h2>What should be included for Dubai businesses?</h2><p>Dubai businesses often need location-aware content, multilingual captions where appropriate, WhatsApp conversion paths, Google profile alignment, seasonal campaign planning, creator coordination and offer testing around Ramadan, Eid, summer, tourist seasons and major local events.</p><h3>For restaurants and hospitality</h3><p>Restaurants need menus, dishes, offers, ambience, review prompts, delivery campaigns and local search support. A dedicated <a href=\"/restaurant-marketing-dubai\">restaurant marketing approach</a> is usually stronger than a generic content calendar.</p><h3>For service businesses</h3><p>Clinics, consultants, real estate firms, salons and B2B companies need proof, explanations, FAQs, founder-led content, case studies, lead forms and high-intent landing pages.</p><h2>What is usually not included?</h2><p>Ad spend, influencer fees, large video shoots, website development, CRM setup and full brand identity work are often separate unless the agreement says otherwise. This matters because a low management fee can become unclear when creative production or paid campaigns are needed later.</p><h2>How to choose a package</h2><p>Pick based on business goal, content volume, production complexity, approval speed, audience language, and whether the agency can connect social to leads or sales. Check whether reporting explains what changed, what worked, and what will be tested next.</p><p>For pricing context, review <a href=\"/pricing\">Talk The Taste pricing</a>. If the issue is that social traffic does not convert, the website may need work through <a href=\"/web-design-dubai\">web design in Dubai</a>.</p>",
